const D53="D53 (R6-LOAD-ESTABLISHMENT, shared with R6-PLANNED-PROGRESSION and R6-ROTATION; found in round 11, made reachable in ordinary use by the D52 (B) fix) r6-program.mjs advanceStrength (after a performed re-establishment the regain restores the state's base set count, priorSets, one set per executed week, without regard to the block-boundary set) and strengthDose (the prescribed count is the base count plus the block-boundary set once blocksDone > 0). After a performed re-establishment at 2 sets the next exposure can be 4 sets at RIR 3: probe AH (72 timelines: FIXED and EVERY_2_WEEKS, four strength goals, strength skipped for 4-6 weeks from week 3, 4 or 5, every week reviewed) finds 120 of 584 next exposures more than one set above the re-establishment. In 72 a block-boundary set earned before the gap returns at once on top of the regained set; in 48 the block whose only executed exposure of the exercise was the re-establishment earns a set that is added in the same week as the regained one, and those 48 also exceed the count prescribed before the gap by more than one set. This contradicts strength.setsAfterReestablishment ('its earlier set count comes back one set per executed week, never at once'), R6-LOAD-ESTABLISHMENT condition 15, R6-PLANNED-PROGRESSION condition 14 and R6-ROTATION condition 10. The logic predates FREEZE-1 (QRE-R6-17 regains the base count only); before D52 (B) a re-establishment after skipped sessions never fired, so it was rarely reachable. Required (runtime only; the declared text already states the intended behaviour): after a performed re-establishment the prescribed set count, including any block-boundary set, rises at most one set per executed week without a phase reduction, from the re-establishment count up to the count the exercise would otherwise have, with phase reductions on top. Add probe AH as regression tests, covering a block-boundary set earned before the gap and one earned by a block whose only executed exposure was the re-establishment. Whether such a block should earn a set at all is a declaration for the next policy revision (R17).";
