 fullTextRetrieved:[{id:'R6-S44',file:'ssctr-evidence/PMC10511399.xml',sha256:fileSha('PMC10511399'),passages:'Abstract; Results (volume reduction by lowering sets; deloading prepares for and allows increased demand in the subsequent cycle); Discussion (consensus definition). Expert opinion: auxiliary, not prescriptive-support eligible.'},{id:'R6-S45',file:'ssctr-evidence/PMC10809978.xml',sha256:fileSha('PMC10809978'),passages:'Abstract; Methods (one week without training at the midpoint, then the same program); Results (strength gains smaller after the deload; size, endurance and power similar); Limitations'},{id:'R6-S46',file:'ssctr-evidence/PMC7496388.xml',sha256:fileSha('PMC7496388'),passages:'Abstract; Results (multivariable models: volume above 32 km/wk and longest run above 21 km with faster half-marathon times, not with more injuries); Discussion limitations (self-report, exclusions, confounding by intrinsic speed)'},{id:'R6-S47',file:'ssctr-evidence/PMC13031491.xml',sha256:fileSha('PMC13031491'),passages:'Abstract; Methods (deload limb: same program except weeks 4 and 8, one session of two sets); Results (no time-by-condition interaction); Limitations'}],
